1
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:04,740
看我又在邮箱里发现了什么
Look what someone left in our mailbox -- again.

2
00:00:04,811 --> 00:00:06,481
等等 这是第五朵了吧
Wait, that's like our fifth one, isn't it?

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:07,620
越来越恐怖了
It's getting kind of creepy.

4
00:00:07,620 --> 00:00:09,380
放松啦 可能是维克托放的
Oh, relax -- it's probably just from Victor,

5
00:00:09,411 --> 00:00:10,901
就是以前跟我约会的送花小哥
that flower-delivery guy I dated.

6
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,380
谁是维克托 我们从没听过他
Who's Victor? We never heard about him.

7
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:13,240
因为我知道你们不会
Oh, because I knew

8
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:14,840
让我跟一个有前科的家伙出去的
you'd never let me go out with an ex-con.

9
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:17,440
也许是迪兰想赢回你的心所以送来的
Hey, maybe it's Dylan trying to win you back.

10
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,200
那么维克托 彻底不可能了吗
So, Victor -- it's a closed door?

11
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,220
可能并不是喜欢海莉的人
Maybe it's not a guy who's in love with Haley.

12
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:23,260
谢谢
Oh, thank you.

13
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:25,060
可能是某个迷恋海莉的家伙
Maybe it's a guy who's obsessed with Haley

14
00:00:25,071 --> 00:00:26,900
于是打算做整形手术 变成她的样子
and is getting plastic surgery to look like her

15
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,420
这样就可以取代她 过她的生活
so he can replace her and live her life.

16
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:29,231
卢克
Luke.

17
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:31,080
就只能是给海莉的吗
So they can only be for Haley?

18
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:31,960
当然不是
Of course not.

19
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:33,760
这里又不是只有海莉一个尤物
Haley isn't the only hottie living here.

20
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:36,600
我前几天穿着我的运动短裤洗车
I washed the car in my cheer shorts the other day.

21
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:37,960
明显感觉到有人在看我
I definitely felt eyes on me.

22
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:41,240
你们就没想过那些花可能是给我的吗
Has it ever occurred to you that those flowers could be for me?

23
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:41,840
什么意思
What do you mean?

24
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,800
我的意思是 也许是我男朋友送的
I mean, like, from my boyfriend.

25
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:44,380
什么
What?

26
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:45,520
你有男朋友了
You have a boyfriend?

27
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,760
你们居然还觉得我的想法不可思议
And you thought my thing was crazy.

28
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:03,030
艾丽克斯 你有男朋友了
Alex, you have a boyfriend?

29
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:05,010
你别就这么撂下一句话就走了啊
You can't just drop that and ave.

30
00:01:05,010 --> 00:01:06,110
亲爱的 太惊喜了
Honey, it is so exciting.

31
00:01:06,110 --> 00:01:07,080
你为什么没告诉我们
Why didn't you tell us?

32
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:08,340
因为我知道你们会觉得很诡异
Because I knew you'd get all weird

33
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:10,040
然后问一堆蠢问题
and ask a million stupid questions.

34
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:11,940
他长什么样 你怎么认识他的
What does he look like? How did you meet him?

35
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:13,000
我给你们看照片
Okay, I'll show you a photo.

36
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:18,920
我是想给你们看 但我手机坏了
Well, I would, but now my phone's not working.

37
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:21,680
对了 这里有他
Oh, here he is.

38
00:01:21,889 --> 00:01:23,219
超市宣传单上嘛
In the supermarket flyer?

39
00:01:23,219 --> 00:01:24,779
就是提着猪排的那个人吗
That's him pondering the pork chops?

40
00:01:24,779 --> 00:01:25,409
有什么好考虑的
What's to ponder?

41
00:01:25,409 --> 00:01:26,739
一磅4.59美元[ponder也有考虑之意]
They're $4.59 a pound.

42
00:01:26,739 --> 00:01:28,049
我不明白 他怎么在这里头
I don't understand. Why is he in this?

43
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:29,460
他是模特 老妈
He's a model, mom.

44
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:31,660
等等 你男友是模特
Oh, wait, wait. Your boyfriend's a model?

45
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:32,980
你怎么认识他的
Well, how did you meet him?

46
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:33,860
全国优秀学生
There's not much crossover

47
00:01:33,899 --> 00:01:36,929
跟猪排模特能有多少交集啊
for a national honor society student and a pork model.

48
00:01:36,929 --> 00:01:39,759
实际上 说来话长 我
Well, actually, it's a really long story. I...

49
00:01:40,849 --> 00:01:42,819
是他的电话
Oh, well -- it's him.

50
00:01:43,139 --> 00:01:44,120
等等
Hey, hold on.

51
00:01:44,499 --> 00:01:45,939
真是太好了
This is terrific news.

52
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:48,020
不敢相信她居然没跟我们说男朋友的事
I can't believe she didn't tell us about him.

53
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:49,720
你不敢相信的就是这个吗
Oh, that's what you can't believe?

54
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:50,579
你什么意思
What do you mean?

55
00:01:50,579 --> 00:01:51,869
菲尔 真有点怪怪的
Phil, it is a little weird.

56
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:53,300
突然之间 她就有了个男朋友
I mean, suddenly she has this boyfriend.

57
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:54,640
她想给我们看手机里的照片
She wants to show us a picture on her phone,

58
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:55,500
但是又没办法
but she can't,

59
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:58,060
然后他又神奇般地出现在了今天的报纸里
and magically he's in today's paper?

60
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:01,280
我都不想说了 海莉
I don't even want to say it. Haley.

61
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:02,420
她肯定是编的
She's making it up.

62
00:02:02,679 --> 00:02:04,009
她为什么这么做
Why would she do that?

63
00:02:04,009 --> 00:02:04,959
可能我们都不相信
Maybe she's upset

64
00:02:04,959 --> 00:02:06,769
那些玫瑰是给她的 让她很伤心
that none of us thought those roses could be for her.

65
00:02:06,769 --> 00:02:07,549
还记得她有一次
Oh, and remember

66
00:02:07,549 --> 00:02:09,319
找不到舞伴参加返校节吗
when she couldn't get a date for homecoming?

67
00:02:09,319 --> 00:02:10,178
她说她不在乎
She said she didn't care,

68
00:02:10,178 --> 00:02:11,598
但我撞见她在她屋里哭来着
but I caught her crying in her room.

69
00:02:11,598 --> 00:02:13,398
亲爱的 你怎么劝的她
Oh, honey, what did you say to her?

70
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:15,780
那天我要迟到了 我也就没...
Oh, I-I was super late, so I didn't really...

71
00:02:15,828 --> 00:02:16,718
太可悲了
This is sad.

72
00:02:16,718 --> 00:02:17,608
艾丽克斯有了天大的喜事
Alex has great news

73
00:02:17,608 --> 00:02:19,278
但她的母亲和姐姐居然不相信她
and her own mother and sister don't believe her?

74
00:02:19,278 --> 00:02:20,028
我也想信她
I want to.

75
00:02:20,028 --> 00:02:21,508
我真的相信她
Well, I do believe her.

76
00:02:21,508 --> 00:02:23,438
我要让她请她男朋友到家里吃晚饭
I'm gonna tell her to invite this boyfriend over for dinner,

77
00:02:23,438 --> 00:02:24,178
我会给你们做一道
and I'll be serving a big,

78
00:02:24,178 --> 00:02:25,808
名叫"早就告诉过你了"的大菜
old platter of "I told you so."

79
00:02:25,808 --> 00:02:26,748
太好了
Oh, great.

80
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,680
你还可以做独角兽汉堡和魔法豆子
Maybe you could also serve unicorn burgers and magic beans,

81
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:31,600
我也要请我男朋友来 野人大脚
and I'll invite my boyfriend, Bigfoot!

82
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:34,040
还是比迪兰好
Still better than Dylan.

83
00:02:35,708 --> 00:02:38,468
来 我给你准备了个惊喜
Okay. I got a surprise for you.

84
00:02:38,468 --> 00:02:40,428
别是又领了个宝宝吧
It better not be another baby.

85
00:02:42,118 --> 00:02:44,378
沙发后面有什么好玩的吗
Is there something fun behind the couch?

86
00:02:44,378 --> 00:02:47,968
埃德加·范德考夫牌的手工特白沙发
An Edgar Vanderkoff hand-crafted blanc de blanc sofa.

87
00:02:47,968 --> 00:02:49,658
是我们给自己的结婚礼物
It was a wedding gift to ourselves.

88
00:02:49,658 --> 00:02:50,828
我们也是在告诉莉莉
Plus, we're showing lily

89
00:02:50,828 --> 00:02:53,378
我们相信她不会破坏这么美的东西
that we trust her enough to let us have one nice thing.

90
00:02:53,378 --> 00:02:54,468
你这么想的话
When you think about it like that,

91
00:02:54,468 --> 00:02:56,938
那真是给莉莉送了份大礼
it's really a gift for Lily. Yeah.

92
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:58,500
好吧
Okay, whoa.

93
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:00,840
只有确定自己是干净的才能坐这沙发
We only get on this couch when we know we're not dirty.

94
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:02,800
所以我们才给她买这个沙发
That's why we got her the couch.

95
00:03:02,807 --> 00:03:04,567
教她懂得尊重
To teach her about respect.

96
00:03:04,687 --> 00:03:06,597
双腿再分开点
Legs a little wider please.

97
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:08,100
你的后兜里是一块饼干吗
Is that a cookie in your back pocket?

98
00:03:08,257 --> 00:03:09,397
-是的 -好吧
- Yep. - Okay.

99
00:03:09,397 --> 00:03:11,347
拿出来 慢点
Bup-up-up! Hey, nice and slow.

100
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:15,760
我正看着呢
Watching that.

101
00:03:16,357 --> 00:03:18,517
既然你在这里 你觉得怎么样
But now that I got you here, what do you think?

102
00:03:19,647 --> 00:03:20,677
之前你穿着大口袋短裤
That you wore cargo shorts

103
00:03:20,820 --> 00:03:22,100
参加我初中毕业仪式
to my middle-school graduation,

104
00:03:22,237 --> 00:03:23,297
去参加狗狗的生日派对
but you're putting on a bow tie

105
00:03:23,297 --> 00:03:24,457
反而戴领结了
for some dog's birthday party.

106
00:03:24,457 --> 00:03:25,407
这是为了好玩啊
It's all good fun.

107
00:03:25,407 --> 00:03:26,787
比恩鲍姆夫妇没法生孩子
The Birnbaums can't have kids.

108
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:28,560
他们想为伯斯特举办一场盛大派对
They like to do it up big for Buster.

109
00:03:28,717 --> 00:03:30,407
我的五岁生日是在一家炸小牛排店的
I had my fifth birthday in a break room

110
00:03:30,407 --> 00:03:32,277
休息室里度过的 但是伯斯特真幸运
of a Der Wienerschnitzel, but good for buster.

111
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:33,560
你怎么这么暴躁
Why are you so cranky?

112
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,800
学校里有个孩子搞金字塔骗局
This kid at school ripped me off for 40 bucks

113
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:39,640
骗了我40块
in a pyramid scheme.

114
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:40,700
那跟你梳妆台上的
Did this have something to do

115
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:43,080
破碎的塑料金字塔有关系吗
with that broken plastic pyramid on your dresser?

116
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:44,660
照片里看起来像是大理石的
It looked like marble in the picture.

117
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:45,420
天啊
Oh, man.

118
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:47,300
我长大时你在哪里啊
Where were you when I was growing up?

119
00:03:47,397 --> 00:03:48,817
你到年级教室之前
I'd have had your dice and cigarettes

120
00:03:48,817 --> 00:03:50,187
我就能骗到你的骰子和香烟
before you got to homeroom.

121
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:51,680
你去哪里上学的 《红男绿女》吗
Where'd you go to school -- "Guys and Dolls"?

122
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,540
虽然你很聪明 但你得更机灵点
Bright as you are, you got to smarten up.

123
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:55,940
你应该更加怀疑别人
You got to be more suspicious of people.

124
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:57,680
不要这么容易受骗了
Stop being such a patsy.

125
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,300
我这身打扮参加派对怎么样
How is this for the party?

126
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:02,320
这是我第一次跟你公园遛狗的朋友们见面
It's my first time meeting your dog-park friends.

127
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:03,700
很棒 但是小心点
Fantastic, but be careful --

128
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:05,480
这圈子里有人还是单身呢
Some of these guys are single in the group.

129
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:06,100
毫不意外
What a surprise.

130
00:04:07,016 --> 00:04:08,706
曼尼 我们不能迟到
Manny, we won't be late.

131
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:10,446
我给你和乔准备了晚餐
I left dinner for you and Joe,

132
00:04:10,446 --> 00:04:12,736
但是不要吃冰箱里的魔鬼蛋
but don't eat the deviled eggs that are in the refrigerator

133
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:14,320
因为那是明天野餐吃的
because they're for tomorrow's picnic.

134
00:04:14,426 --> 00:04:16,306
什么野餐 庆祝某人的猫上大学了吗
What picnic -- somebody's cat going to college?

135
00:04:16,306 --> 00:04:18,726
不是 歌洛莉亚的一些朋友拿到了绿卡
No, some of Gloria's friends are getting their green cards.

136
00:04:18,726 --> 00:04:20,107
他们其实人很好
It's actually a nice group.

137
00:04:20,126 --> 00:04:22,456
是啊 他们是认真工作的正派人
Yes, they're very decent, hardworking people.

138
00:04:22,456 --> 00:04:24,746
杰在米拉贝拉的假婚礼上遇见了他们
Jay met them at Mirabelle's fake wedding.

139
00:04:24,746 --> 00:04:25,817
《祖宝》
Zooboo!

140
00:04:25,826 --> 00:04:28,686
不 今天你已经看了六次《祖宝》
No, you've already watched "Zooboo" six times today.

141
00:04:28,686 --> 00:04:29,766
我们要在大屏幕上
We're gonna watch a classic movie

142
00:04:29,766 --> 00:04:31,026
看一部经典电影
right here on the big screen.

143
00:04:31,026 --> 00:04:32,636
你最好让他看他的节目
You better let him watch his show.

144
00:04:32,636 --> 00:04:33,826
不然他会炸毛的
If not, he's gonna freak out.

145
00:04:33,826 --> 00:04:34,906
昨天我关了电视
Yesterday I turned it off,

146
00:04:34,906 --> 00:04:37,006
他咬穿了一颗台球
and he bit through one of the pool balls.

147
00:04:44,836 --> 00:04:45,716
米奇尔
Hey, Mitchell.

148
00:04:45,716 --> 00:04:47,515
你好啊
Hi, uh, um...

149
00:04:47,525 --> 00:04:49,015
布...伦达
B...renda.

150
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:51,500
你还以为我不记得了 对吧
Yes, you thought I wasn't gonna remember, didn't you?

151
00:04:51,585 --> 00:04:53,495
上班第一周感觉怎么样
So, how's your first week been?

152
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:54,560
我要离婚了
I'm getting a divorce.

153
00:04:54,980 --> 00:04:55,960
天啊
Oh. God.

154
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:58,420
是我问的 所以...
Um...well, I did ask, so...

155
00:04:58,555 --> 00:05:00,195
我不想一个人待着 懂吗
It's really hard to be alone, you know?

156
00:05:00,195 --> 00:05:01,286
懂
Yeah.

157
00:05:01,805 --> 00:05:04,565
你知道还有谁也加班吗 史黛丝
Hey, you know who else who stays late is, um, Stacey.

158
00:05:04,565 --> 00:05:06,095
-14个月了 -天啊
- 14 months. - Oh, gosh.

159
00:05:06,095 --> 00:05:08,365
有时候早点抽身也挺好的
Well, sometimes it's good to get in and out fast, though, huh?

160
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:10,300
我们14个月没做爱了
We haven't had sex in 14 months.

161
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:12,200
我们结婚20年了
We were married 20 years.

162
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:13,740
这个数字不错
Well, that's a nice, round number.

163
00:05:13,895 --> 00:05:14,655
是的
Yeah.

164
00:05:14,655 --> 00:05:17,965
我的不宁腿综合症 这是离开的原因吗
My restless leg syndrome, like that's a reason to leave?

165
00:05:18,095 --> 00:05:19,145
你知道 大家都有...
Well, you know, everybody has --

166
00:05:19,145 --> 00:05:22,195
他有好多恶习和无理要求
Especially after all his habits and requests!

167
00:05:22,195 --> 00:05:24,135
我比刘易斯和克拉克远征时
God! I've done more paddling

168
00:05:24,260 --> 00:05:25,740
"划船"划得都多
than Lewis and Clark!

169
00:05:26,625 --> 00:05:27,975
史黛丝 你在吗
Hey, Stace, you out there?

170
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:30,140
她走了 人们会离开
Oh, she's gone. People leave.

171
00:05:30,305 --> 00:05:32,115
如果我可以做点什么
Well, you know, i-if there's anything

172
00:05:32,115 --> 00:05:33,625
来帮助你
that I can do to help you --

173
00:05:33,625 --> 00:05:34,685
我能和你待在一起吗
Could I stay with you?

174
00:05:34,685 --> 00:05:35,506
什么
What's that?

175
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:39,940
拉里可以坐在沙发上 而我不行吗
So, Larry's allowed to sit on the couch and I'm not?

176
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:41,680
拉里是白色的[白人]
Well, Larry is white.

177
00:05:41,804 --> 00:05:43,164
是你们选择的我
Hey, you chose me.

178
00:05:43,164 --> 00:05:45,494
我不是那个意思
Oh, uh, that's not what I meant.

179
00:05:47,834 --> 00:05:49,604
-喂 -好啊 小卡
- Hello? - Hey, Cam.

180
00:05:49,604 --> 00:05:50,374
你记得
So, listen, you remember

181
00:05:50,374 --> 00:05:52,774
我的新同事布伦达对吧
my -- my new friend at work Brenda, right?

182
00:05:52,774 --> 00:05:53,434
谁
Who?

183
00:05:53,434 --> 00:05:55,164
是啊 那个美女
That's right -- the pretty one.

184
00:05:55,164 --> 00:05:58,364
她和她丈夫在闹矛盾
Uh, so, she and her husband are -- are going through some problems at home,

185
00:05:58,440 --> 00:05:59,060
她想知道
and she was wondering

186
00:05:59,060 --> 00:06:01,120
是否可以暂住在我们家
if she might be able to stay at our house.

187
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,900
天哪 当然可以了
Oh, my gosh. Yes, of course.

188
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:04,960
对了 该死
Oh, shoot and darn it!

189
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:05,770
我就记得好像有什么事的
I thought we had something.

190
00:06:06,294 --> 00:06:08,134
米奇尔 我知道你在干什么
Mitchell, I know what you're doing.

191
00:06:08,134 --> 00:06:10,744
没办法改期了 对吧
Ahh, there's no way we can reschedule, huh?

192
00:06:10,744 --> 00:06:11,564
战胜你的本能
Fight your instincts.

193
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:13,820
这是你表现同情心的机会
This is a chance for you to show some real compassion.

194
00:06:14,924 --> 00:06:17,594
-我要吃左洛复[抗抑郁药] -好 好
- I need a zoloft. - Okay. Okay.

195
00:06:17,594 --> 00:06:18,974
你说的我都同意
Well, I agree with all that,

196
00:06:18,974 --> 00:06:21,034
不过 我已经很客气了
but I -- I am being nice!

197
00:06:21,034 --> 00:06:23,534
好吗 我跟她说话
Okay? I -- I-I-I talked to her.

198
00:06:23,534 --> 00:06:25,394
我还问她 有什么我能帮忙的地方
I-I asked her if there was anything I could do to help.

199
00:06:25,394 --> 00:06:26,624
可是 我不是认真的
But I -- I didn't mean it.

200
00:06:26,624 --> 00:06:27,774
谁也不可能是认真的
Nobody ever means it.

201
00:06:27,774 --> 00:06:29,484
米奇尔 你希望自己在这方面有长进的
Mitchell, you want this growth in your life.

202
00:06:29,484 --> 00:06:31,644
所以你才会问她 你只是害怕而已
That's why you asked her. You're just scared.

203
00:06:31,644 --> 00:06:34,913
不 不是 那完全就是个虚伪的提议
No, no, it was a completely hollow offer and --

204
00:06:34,913 --> 00:06:35,853
是的 没错
Yeah, that -- that's right.

205
00:06:35,853 --> 00:06:37,093
好的 乔治和温蒂·哈洛请我们
Okay, George and Wendy Hollow offer

206
00:06:37,093 --> 00:06:38,463
晚上七点半吃晚餐 好的 再见
dinner at 7:30. Okay, bye-bye.

207
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:40,480
你需要做这件好事 而我也需要它
You need this, and I need something nice

208
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:42,120
作为可以写在圣诞卡片上的素材
to write about you in our Christmas Letter.

209
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,860
我也爱你 再见
I love you, too. Goodbye.

210
00:06:44,143 --> 00:06:46,793
坏消息 是吗
So...bad news, huh?

211
00:06:48,660 --> 00:06:50,580
是啊 如果你介意吃家常菜的话
Well, only if you hate home cooking.

212
00:06:52,803 --> 00:06:54,104
-你是最好的 -那就
- You're the best! - So --

213
00:06:55,873 --> 00:06:57,613
你好像吃进去一点我的左洛复了
I think you got some of my zoloft.

214
00:06:57,613 --> 00:06:58,954
没关系 我用得上
That's okay. I could use it.

215
00:07:04,853 --> 00:07:06,823
狗狗的成年礼 这概念太好了
Bark Mitzvah -- what a concept.

216
00:07:06,823 --> 00:07:09,323
贝狗饼夹熏鱼 狗胸饼
Beagles and lox, dog briskets.

217
00:07:09,323 --> 00:07:12,183
负责这些文字游戏的人真是太赞了
Whoever's in charge of the wordplay, bravo.

218
00:07:12,223 --> 00:07:13,613
这是给狗吃的还是给人吃的
Is this for dogs or for people?

219
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:15,640
希望是给人吃的 我都吃了四块了
I hope it's for people. I've had four of them.

220
00:07:15,973 --> 00:07:17,793
-你觉得有意思吗 -是的
- Are you having fun? - Ay, yes.

221
00:07:17,793 --> 00:07:21,283
今天前 我还从没见过肉汁喷泉
Before today, I had never seen a gravy fountain.

222
00:07:21,433 --> 00:07:24,982
小软糖 快看 斯黛拉来了
Oh, Gumdrop, look! Stella's here!

223
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:27,100
大家快来 我们照张合影
Everybody, let's get a picture.

224
00:07:28,312 --> 00:07:30,592
还有狗仔队呢 太棒了
Pupparazzi! How great is that?

225
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,080
大家靠近一点
Everybody squeeze in.

226
00:07:33,642 --> 00:07:35,382
小心她的包囊 她会咬你的
Be careful of her cysts. She'll nip you.

227
00:07:35,382 --> 00:07:36,252
好的
O-okay.

228
00:07:36,252 --> 00:07:38,362
好的 再来一张 小涂鸦刚才眨眼了
Okay, one more. Doodles blinked.

229
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:40,400
这次靠得再近一些
Now, really get tight this time.

230
00:07:40,822 --> 00:07:41,972
不 不 不
No! No, no, no!

231
00:07:41,972 --> 00:07:44,442
-够了 够了 -歌洛莉亚 歌洛莉亚
- Enough. Enough. - Oh, Gloria -- Gloria.

232
00:07:44,742 --> 00:07:45,882
歌洛莉亚 亲爱的
Gloria, honey, I -- listen.

233
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:47,052
我知道你不喜欢狗
I-I know you're not a dog person.

234
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,440
不是 跟狗在一起没问题
No, I'm okay with the dogs.

235
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:50,880
我只是不喜欢爱狗的那些人
I'm just not a dog-person person.

236
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:53,980
你说这个派对是正常的
You said that this party was going to be normal.

237
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:55,120
只是图个乐子
It's just fun.

238
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:57,940
这有个为狗准备的自助餐和酒吧
There's a buffet and an open bar for dogs.

239
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:00,340
我表亲在救生艇上结的婚
My cousin got married on a raft.

240
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:02,300
我很努力地融入了 杰
I tried to play along, Jay,

241
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:03,660
但这也太疯狂了
but -- but this is crazy.

242
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:05,160
我必须要回家了
I have to go home.

243
00:08:05,242 --> 00:08:06,482
歌洛莉亚 你认为用疯狂这个词
Gloria, now, do you think it's fair

244
00:08:06,482 --> 00:08:08,602
来形容这里公平吗
to use the word "Crazy" about a --

245
00:08:11,862 --> 00:08:13,582
我们回家见 歌洛莉亚
I-I'll see you at home, Gloria.

246
00:08:15,962 --> 00:08:18,211
非常感谢你们
Oh, thank you so much, you guys.

247
00:08:18,211 --> 00:08:19,161
天哪 我寻找真命天子的时候
God, where were you when I was

248
00:08:19,161 --> 00:08:20,661
你们在哪呢
looking for the perfect man?

249
00:08:20,661 --> 00:08:21,751
可能在密苏里
Well, probably in Missouri

250
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:23,011
一家叫堪萨斯城肉棒的酒吧
at a bar called Kansas City Meats

251
00:08:23,060 --> 00:08:24,800
-做着同样的事吧 -太幽默了
- doing the same thing. - Funny!

252
00:08:26,431 --> 00:08:28,201
-看你笑得 -怎么了
- Look at that smile. - What?

253
00:08:28,201 --> 00:08:30,541
这就是表达善意的感觉
That's what being nice feels like.

254
00:08:30,541 --> 00:08:32,511
-我很喜欢 -我为你骄傲
- I like it. - I'm proud of you.

255
00:08:32,511 --> 00:08:33,671
我只是让一个不怎么认识的人
Well, I'm just letting a person

256
00:08:33,671 --> 00:08:35,081
住在我的家里
I barely know sleep in my home.

257
00:08:35,081 --> 00:08:36,771
我不知道是否可以称得上是英雄 可是
I don't know if I'd use the word "Hero," But...

258
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:37,240
英雄
"Hero"?

259
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:39,140
别说了 我都不好意思了
Stop it. You're embarrassing me.

260
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:42,160
天哪
Oh, god.

261
00:08:43,491 --> 00:08:45,031
你们养猫了吗
Hey, you guys have a cat?

262
00:08:45,031 --> 00:08:47,151
我给你加点酒吧
Um, how about I freshen up that wine, huh?

263
00:08:47,151 --> 00:08:48,481
不用 我很好 好吧
Oh, no. I am good. Okay, um...

264
00:08:48,481 --> 00:08:49,421
事实上 小卡 我们
In fact, Cam, what are --

265
00:08:49,421 --> 00:08:51,881
我们在客厅里待着干什么呢
what are we doing in the living room, here?

266
00:08:51,881 --> 00:08:52,451
你知道吗
You know?

267
00:08:52,451 --> 00:08:53,291
是啊 知道吗
Yeah, oh, you know what?

268
00:08:53,291 --> 00:08:55,201
我们还没带布伦达参观我们的车库呢
We haven't even given Brenda a tour of our ga-- uh, garage.

269
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:56,001
我们的车库
Our -- our gage.

270
00:08:56,260 --> 00:08:57,200
不去了 我不喜欢车库
Oh, no. I don't like garages.

271
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:59,420
道格把他心爱的帆船就放在车库里
That's where Doug kept his precious sailboat.

272
00:08:59,420 --> 00:09:00,980
不许在船上吃东西
No eating on the boat.

273
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:02,120
不许在船上喝酒
No drinking on the boat.

274
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:04,420
就因为有一次我在船上把酒撒了
All because the one time I went on the boat, I spilled.

275
00:09:04,461 --> 00:09:07,151
-知道吗 船上就是这样 -老天
- Well, guess what. Boats go like this. - Oh, geez.

276
00:09:07,291 --> 00:09:09,261
你知道吗 我当时...
You know?! And I'm like...

277
00:09:10,340 --> 00:09:13,580
谁会爱惜一样东西多过爱惜一个人
Who -- who loves a thing more than a person?

278
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:14,560
禽兽
A monster.

279
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:16,800
我们带你看我们的小棚子了吗
Have we shown you our shed?

280
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:17,480
我们有个小棚子
There's a shed.

281
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:20,260
他跟我结婚的时候就知道我是什么样的
He knew what he was getting into when he married me.

282
00:09:20,260 --> 00:09:21,920
我有点悲剧
I'm a little messy.

283
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:24,460
没想到吧 道格
Well, guess what, Doug!

284
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:25,960
生活本来就是个杯具
Life's a little messy.

285
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:29,260
我鼻水流个不停 耳朵也会渗出液体
Okay, my sinuses leak, my -- my ears run,

286
00:09:29,260 --> 00:09:31,960
我的汗腺还过度发达
and I have hyperactive sweat glands, but...

287
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:34,640
我确实需要再来一杯
You know what? I do need a refill.

288
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:38,760
我一点也不吃惊 她失了不少水
Well, I'm not surprised. She's losing a lot of fluids.

289
00:09:38,760 --> 00:09:40,720
就像道格就在这里一样
It's as if Doug was over here.

290
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:41,580
我知道 我看到了
I know. I saw that.

291
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,160
艾丽克
Alec!

292
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:47,880
他的二货爸爸被调去非洲
His dumb dad got transferred to dumb Africa

293
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:49,380
给一些二货孩子看病
to operate on some dumb babies.

294
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:52,660
去给他们治心脏就要伤我的心吗
So fixing their hearts is worth breaking mine?

295
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:54,200
还是挺值得的
It's kind of worth it.

296
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:56,120
他每天可以做六台手术
He can do like six operations a day.

297
00:09:56,270 --> 00:09:58,610
是 我理解 不好意思我冲你发火了
Yeah. I-I-I understand. I'm sorry I'm lashing out.

298
00:09:58,610 --> 00:10:01,250
我只是太喜欢你了
I-I just really like you.

299
00:10:01,250 --> 00:10:02,819
我还喜欢你
I still like you.

300
00:10:02,989 --> 00:10:04,550
你这么说我感觉更糟
You're making this worse.

301
00:10:05,399 --> 00:10:06,460
再见 艾丽克
Bye, Alec.

302
00:10:06,559 --> 00:10:07,530
再见 艾丽克斯
Bye, Alex.

303
00:10:09,809 --> 00:10:11,639
我就知道你不最后亲我一下是不会走的
I knew you couldn't leave without one last kiss!

304
00:10:11,639 --> 00:10:13,339
我们可以解决这个问题
We can work this out!

305
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:16,830
我 我会后悔的 对吧
I'm -- I'm -- I'm gonna regret that, aren't I?

306
00:10:17,339 --> 00:10:19,719
我只是想让你帮我丢一下这个
Uh, I was hoping you could throw this away for me.

307
00:10:23,420 --> 00:10:24,500
好 当然
Yeah. Sure.

308
00:10:28,560 --> 00:10:31,500
亲爱的 我们聊了一下
So, honey, we've been talking,

309
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:33,080
都想见见你男朋友
and we want to meet your boyfriend.

310
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:35,020
你们刚错过了
You just missed him.

311
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:36,360
他来了吗
He was here?

312
00:10:36,429 --> 00:10:39,549
他刚走 这是他的杯子
He just left. This is his cup.

313
00:10:39,549 --> 00:10:41,799
瞧瞧这个
Oh, look at that.

314
00:10:41,869 --> 00:10:44,299
这看着像"艾丽克斯"
Oh, it looks like "Alex."

315
00:10:44,299 --> 00:10:47,189
他名叫艾丽克 那个"C"被抹花了
His name is Alec. The "C" Just got smudged.

316
00:10:47,349 --> 00:10:49,169
亲 他叫艾丽克
Honey, his name is Alec.

317
00:10:49,169 --> 00:10:50,109
但那个"C"被抹花了
But the "C" Got smudged.

318
00:10:50,109 --> 00:10:51,899
对了 你怎么不给他发个短信
Yeah, um, well, why don't you just text him

319
00:10:51,899 --> 00:10:53,429
邀请他来吃晚饭
and then invite him back for dinner?

320
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:55,260
不行 他跟我分手了
I can't. He broke up with me.

321
00:10:55,620 --> 00:10:56,800
不是吧
Oh, no.

322
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:59,340
他要搬去非洲
He's moving to Africa.

323
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:01,840
因为非洲的超市需要模特
Because they need grocery models in Africa.

324
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:03,780
亲爱的 我很遗憾
Honey, I'm so sorry.

325
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:04,840
他们分手了
They broke up.

326
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:07,000
我想他
I miss him.

327
00:11:07,560 --> 00:11:08,560
别担心
Oh, don't worry.

328
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:11,060
很快他就像从没出现过一样了
Soon it will be like he never existed.

329
00:11:12,538 --> 00:11:13,459
好了
Okay.

330
00:11:13,688 --> 00:11:16,278
我的天啊 曼尼 乔怎么了
Ay dios mío, Manny, what's going on with Joe?

331
00:11:16,278 --> 00:11:17,608
他就是个瘾君子
He's a drug addict.

332
00:11:17,608 --> 00:11:20,308
看了两个小时的白痴剧《祖宝》以后
After two hours of mind-liquefying "Zooboo,"

333
00:11:20,308 --> 00:11:23,078
我只是放了一部老电影 他就暴走了
I briefly put on a classic movie, and he freaked out.

334
00:11:23,178 --> 00:11:24,228
要是他走得再稳一点
If he could walk better,

335
00:11:24,228 --> 00:11:25,998
我肯定要推荐个戒毒项目给他
I'd seriously suggest a 12-step program.

336
00:11:25,998 --> 00:11:28,808
不要 乔 不看《祖宝》了
Ay, no, Joe. No more "Zooboo."

337
00:11:28,808 --> 00:11:29,458
谢谢
Thank you.

338
00:11:29,458 --> 00:11:32,008
不要 把大电视关掉
Ay, no. Turn the big TV off.

339
00:11:32,008 --> 00:11:35,258
他看到电视开着就会要看他想看的节目
If he sees it on, he's going to want to watch his show.

340
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:38,000
你怎么回来了
Why are you home?

341
00:11:38,188 --> 00:11:40,798
伯斯特的派对是个给狗办的犹太成人礼
Buster's party was a bark mitzvah.

342
00:11:40,798 --> 00:11:43,638
我搞不懂杰怎么会带我去那里
I don't know why Jay would take me to this place.

343
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:44,980
我不知道
I don't know.

344
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:46,760
也许狗狗派对什么的
Maybe this dog stuff is his way

345
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:48,460
只是他想找点跟你的共同兴趣
of trying to find a common interest with you.

346
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:49,560
这不容易
It's hard.

347
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:51,920
你不喜欢高尔夫或威士忌
You don't like golf or scotch

348
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:53,380
或者艾森豪威尔的纪录片
or Eisenhower documentaries.

349
00:11:53,447 --> 00:11:55,297
没错 我不喜欢艾克
It's true. I don't like Ike.

350
00:11:55,397 --> 00:11:56,447
可是这个派对上的人
But the people in this party,

351
00:11:56,447 --> 00:11:58,287
他们对狗简直痴迷
they are so obsessed with dogs.

352
00:11:58,287 --> 00:12:01,597
连酒杯都是马桶形状的
Even the punch bowl was in the shape of a toilet.

353
00:12:01,597 --> 00:12:03,097
杰又不是
Well, it's not like Jay

354
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:04,860
不会为了你做自己不愿做的事
doesn't get out of his comfort zone for you.

355
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:06,820
他明天要去你的绿卡野餐
He's going to your green-card picnic tomorrow.

356
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:08,380
你说得对
You're right.

357
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:11,960
他还给所有人买了带星星的墨西哥宽边帽
He even bought star-spangled sombreros for everybody.

358
00:12:12,177 --> 00:12:13,197
他弄错国家了
It's the wrong country.

359
00:12:13,197 --> 00:12:16,237
他从来不听我说话 不过他很贴心
He never listens, but -- but he's sweet.

360
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:17,640
你知道吗
You know what?

361
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:19,920
我该回那个派对去
I should go back to that party.

362
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:22,540
你们想来吗
You guys want to come?

363
00:12:22,660 --> 00:12:23,480
倒也无妨
Might as well.

364
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:25,420
我记得伯斯特的割礼上果酱挺好吃的
They had a pretty good spread at Buster's bris.

365
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:28,080
好了 我们把这个女人弄到床上去
Okay, let's get this woman into bed

366
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:30,600
明天一早 用最快的速度让她离开
and, in the morning, out of the house as fast as we can.

367
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:32,340
说实话 我不知道直男是怎么做到的
Honestly, I don't know how straight guys do it.

368
00:12:32,340 --> 00:12:33,900
大概没有这么多手势吧
Probably without those hand gestures.

369
00:12:35,037 --> 00:12:36,307
洗得好吗
So, nice bath?

370
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:38,980
太舒服了 我准备好上床睡觉了
the best. I'm so ready for bed.

371
00:12:39,117 --> 00:12:41,126
哦对了 我留了个环在里面
Okay. Ooh, by the way, I left a ring in there.

372
00:12:41,126 --> 00:12:43,176
没事 我们明早漂白一下就好了
Oh, well, we'll get at it with some bleach in the morning.

373
00:12:43,176 --> 00:12:44,256
不 不是 是我的婚戒
No, no, no, my wedding ring.

374
00:12:44,256 --> 00:12:45,596
我只是不想再戴着它了
I just don't feel like wearing it anymore.

375
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:47,300
和讨厌的回忆说再见
Oh, well, goodbye, bad memories,

376
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:49,700
迎接我们的客用沙发 云端
hello to our guest couch, the Cloud.

377
00:12:51,066 --> 00:12:52,286
真是个小云端
That's a small cloud.

378
00:12:52,286 --> 00:12:54,196
你知道吗 它舒服极了
Oh, you know what? It's deceptively comfy.

379
00:12:54,196 --> 00:12:55,426
我经常在那上面睡觉
I sleep on it all the time.

380
00:12:55,426 --> 00:12:56,806
-是啊 如果我没抢赢他 -真的吗
- Yeah, if I don't beat him to it first. - Really?

381
00:12:56,806 --> 00:12:59,066
好吧 就这样
Oh, okay. All right.

382
00:12:59,066 --> 00:12:59,876
你躺下了
So, there you are.

383
00:12:59,876 --> 00:13:00,996
-好了 -好了 是的
- Okay. - Okay, yeah.

384
00:13:00,996 --> 00:13:02,936
我不...我很确定这不行啊
I'm not -- I'm pretty sure this isn't gonna work.

385
00:13:02,936 --> 00:13:04,466
不 这没事的 没事的
No, no, this will be fine. This will be fine.

386
00:13:04,466 --> 00:13:06,076
我总是这样做的 没什么大不了
This is what I always do. It's not a big deal.

387
00:13:06,260 --> 00:13:07,800
给你布置得舒服一点
Just make this up nice for you.

388
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:09,000
这样就好了
There we go. Okay.

389
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:09,980
明早见
See you in the morning.

390
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:11,500
可是我的 我的头
Yeah, but my -- my head's --

391
00:13:12,076 --> 00:13:13,546
看我们都在想什么呢
Oh. What we were thinking?

392
00:13:13,546 --> 00:13:14,426
来吧 这样就好了
Here. Come on. There it is right there.

393
00:13:14,426 --> 00:13:16,356
-睡吧 晚安 -晚安
- There you go. Okay. Night-night. - Night-night.

394
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:17,100
两位
Hey, guys.

395
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:19,020
我有个主意
Here's an idea.

396
00:13:19,020 --> 00:13:21,600
我睡到你们客厅的那个沙发上怎么样
What if I just slept on your couch in the living room?

397
00:13:27,900 --> 00:13:28,840
我在发抖
I'm shaking.

398
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:30,240
怎么了 问题解决了
Why? Problem solved.

399
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:32,580
不是 她的呼噜声让整个房子都在抖
No, she's making the whole house shake.

400
00:13:40,660 --> 00:13:43,200
你们回来了 出什么事了
Hey, guys. You're back? What's going on?

401
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:47,200
对不起 我爱你 而你喜欢这狗派对
I'm sorry. I love you, and you love dog parties.

402
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:49,560
这就意味着我也喜欢狗派对
So that means that I love dog parties.

403
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:50,940
你不再认为这很疯狂了吗
You don't think it's crazy anymore?

404
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:52,800
我没那么说
I didn't say that.

405
00:13:53,265 --> 00:13:54,775
不过曼尼说得对
But Manny's right.

406
00:13:54,925 --> 00:13:58,105
我们应该多参与一下对方的社交活动
We should get more involved in each other's activities.

407
00:13:58,380 --> 00:13:59,840
这是你的主意吗
So, this was your idea?

408
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:02,380
这应该是健康婚姻生活的基础
Well, it's sort of the foundation of any healthy marriage,

409
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:03,420
不过是我提出来的
but I did bring it up.

410
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:04,480
这太棒了
This is great!

411
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:05,920
来吧 给我搭把手
Well, come on. Give me a hand.

412
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:07,760
我们给你和你妈妈弄个冰淇淋骨头尝尝
We'll grab you and your mom an ice-cream bone.

413
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:11,040
我真的没做什么 我只是
I didn't do much. I just --

414
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:12,160
毁了我的计划 仅此而已
Ruined my plan, that's all.

415
00:14:12,160 --> 00:14:13,060
我希望她离开的
I wanted her to leave!

416
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:13,440
什么
What?

417
00:14:13,675 --> 00:14:15,305
她本应该怒气冲冲离开这里
She was supposed to storm out of here.

418
00:14:15,305 --> 00:14:17,295
然后 等我回家就可以说
And after, I go home and say,

419
00:14:17,295 --> 00:14:19,295
"也许我们应该分头做事"
"Maybe we should do some things separately."

420
00:14:19,295 --> 00:14:21,665
这样我明天就有借口
I was gonna use her bailing out of this

421
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:24,580
推掉那个愚蠢的野餐了
as a chip to get out of that stupid picnic tomorrow.

422
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:25,940
可是现在我没有借口了
But now I've got no chip.

423
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:27,880
下次你计划想逃避什么的时候
Hey, how about next time you devise a plan

424
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:30,040
能不能给我点暗示
to avoid expressing a feeling, clue me in.

425
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:32,240
我不能给你暗示 你脑子太不好使了
You can't be clued in. You're a patsy.

426
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,620
刚才不是说要弄冰淇淋骨头吗
There was talk of an ice-cream bone?

427
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:38,420
那是我编的 动动脑子好不好
I made that up, too. Use your head!

428
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:41,420
亲爱的 你一个人吗
Hey, honey, you alone?

429
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:44,220
你在这里看到别人了吗
Do you see anyone else in here?

430
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:45,540
你呢
Do you?

431
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:49,020
宝贝 你爸爸和我觉得该跟你道歉
Sweetheart, your father and I think we owe you an apology.

432
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:50,340
为了什么
For what?

433
00:14:50,740 --> 00:14:51,880
今早 我们都没想到
Well, this morning when we didn't think

434
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:52,940
玫瑰花可能是送给你的
the rose could be for you,

435
00:14:52,940 --> 00:14:54,700
看起来有点伤你的心了
it seemed like maybe it hurt your feelings.

436
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:55,920
我想是有一点
I guess. A little.

437
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:58,640
我很抱歉让你难受了
I am so sorry to make you feel bad.

438
00:14:58,640 --> 00:14:59,880
你拥有追求者
And it is completely believable

439
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:01,460
是完全有可能的
that you would have an admirer.

440
00:15:01,460 --> 00:15:02,180
好吧
Okay.

441
00:15:02,460 --> 00:15:03,580
我们担心的是
What we're worried about

442
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:05,380
我们营造出来的这种氛围
is that we have created an environment

443
00:15:05,380 --> 00:15:07,340
让你觉得有必要...
in which you feel it's necessary to...

444
00:15:08,214 --> 00:15:09,274
-修... -虚...
- embelli-- - fanta--

445
00:15:09,274 --> 00:15:10,804
-夸... -天哪
- exagger-- - Oh, my god.

446
00:15:10,804 --> 00:15:12,574
你们认为艾丽克是我虚构出来的吗
You guys don't think Alec is real?

447
00:15:12,574 --> 00:15:14,844
宝贝 我还记得在高中的时候
Sweetheart, I remember the pressure there was

448
00:15:14,844 --> 00:15:16,124
所承受的那些压力
to fit in in high school.

449
00:15:16,124 --> 00:15:17,913
我也是 不管你是
So do I. And whether you try to fit in

450
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:19,540
编造说你跟小熊打过架
by saying you fought a baby bear

451
00:15:19,540 --> 00:15:21,280
还是虚构一个男朋友
or by making up a boyfriend...

452
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:23,200
你们俩真不可理喻
You guys are so unbelievable.

453
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,900
你们真的觉得我悲催到
You really think I'm that pathetic

454
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:27,300
要编造个幻想男友出来吗
that I'd have to create some imaginary boyfriend?

455
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:28,920
你知道什么不是幻想出来的吗
You know what's not imaginary?

456
00:15:29,673 --> 00:15:30,503
你的情感
Your feelings.

457
00:15:30,503 --> 00:15:31,863
别 别碰我
Okay, don't! Don't!

458
00:15:31,863 --> 00:15:33,233
告诉你们吧 我刚在Facebook上
F.Y.I., I changed my Facebook

459
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:34,020
把情感状况改成单身
status to "single"

460
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:35,820
才改了一个小时 你们猜怎么着
about an hour ago, and guess what.

461
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,280
已经有人约我了
I already have a date.

462
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:38,960
你们不信我 是不是
You don't believe me, do you?

463
00:15:39,023 --> 00:15:40,983
亲爱的 半分钟内你已经交了两个男友
Sweetheart, you've had two boyfriends in 30 seconds.

464
00:15:40,983 --> 00:15:42,523
几乎破了海莉的纪录
That practically Haley's record.

465
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:44,780
他是真实存在的 他叫泰迪
Well, he's real. His name is Teddy.

466
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:46,940
他叫泰迪[熊]吗
His name is...Teddy?

467
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:48,440
是啊
Yeah.

468
00:15:49,533 --> 00:15:50,974
泰迪·凯斯[钥匙]
Teddy Keyes.

469
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:54,820
这个年轻人是怎么样一个人
And what do we know about this young man?

470
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,700
他是新转来我们学校的
He's new to our school.

471
00:15:56,753 --> 00:16:00,333
在一个叫"床垫大王"的店打工[马丁·路德·金]
He works at some mattress store -- Mattress King.

472
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:02,080
还有就是他有些坏男生气质
And he's a bit of a bad boy.

473
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:03,820
他过去在商店里偷过东西
He had a little problem with shoplifting.

474
00:16:03,820 --> 00:16:05,360
在少管所待过一阵
He spent some time in juvie.

475
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:07,520
不过说实话 他不太是我的菜
But, you know, he's not really my type.

476
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:08,320
就是过渡期的备胎罢了
He's just a rebound.

477
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:09,740
所以我觉得应该无所谓吧
So I guess it doesn't really matter.

478
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:11,900
我为什么要告诉你们这些
Why am I even talking to you guys?

479
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:12,700
快走[树叶]
Leave!

480
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:15,520
赶紧走
Get out!

481
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:20,740
你看到她的眼神了吗
Did you see the look in her eyes?

482
00:16:20,740 --> 00:16:22,640
就好像她真的相信她说的一样
Like she believed everything she was saying.

483
00:16:22,692 --> 00:16:24,812
太恐怖了 就好像我大学认识的一个人
That's terrifying. Like this guy I knew in college.

484
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:26,760
他老是给我讲这些疯狂派对
He was always telling me about these "crazy parties"

485
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:27,600
说那里到处都是女的
that were "full of women."

486
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:28,660
可每次我问他派对在哪里
But when I'd ask him where they were,

487
00:16:28,660 --> 00:16:30,260
他都会给我假地址
he'd give me a fake address.

488
00:16:30,662 --> 00:16:32,562
这让我疑惑究竟还有什么是她编出来的
Makes me wonder what else she's making up.

489
00:16:32,562 --> 00:16:34,762
我从来没见过她辅导数学的那个女生
I have never met that girl she turtors in math.

490
00:16:34,762 --> 00:16:36,112
埃丝特·蔡吗 我也没见过
Esther Choi? Me neither.

491
00:16:36,112 --> 00:16:37,452
因为她根本就不存在
Because she doesn't exist!

492
00:16:37,452 --> 00:16:39,162
这世上没有一个叫埃丝特·蔡[华裔]
There is not an Esther Choi on earth

493
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,260
还需要被辅导数学的
who needs math tutoring.

494
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:41,300
她需要帮助 克莱尔
She needs help, Claire.

495
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:42,440
我们该怎么办
What do we do?

496
00:16:42,452 --> 00:16:44,232
我们该再送她去看那个心理医生吗
I mean, should we send her back to that therapist?

497
00:16:44,232 --> 00:16:45,502
我们从没见过的那个吗
The one we've never met?

498
00:16:45,860 --> 00:16:47,020
不 等等
No! Wait!

499
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:48,520
别开门 让开
Don't open it! Move away!

500
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:50,280
是找我的 让开
It's for me! Move!

501
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,920
天啊 你好漂亮
Damn. You look hot.

502
00:16:55,920 --> 00:16:57,460
玫瑰是你送的吗 泰迪
The roses are from you, Teddy?

503
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:59,800
是啊 我在少管所认识个人在墓地工作
Yeah, I met a guy in juvie who works at the cemetery.

504
00:16:59,900 --> 00:17:01,540
他们那儿到处都是花
They got flowers all over the place.

505
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:03,840
我还给你带了这个
Oh, I also got you this.

506
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:05,620
太棒了 走吧
Sweet. Let's go.

507
00:17:05,751 --> 00:17:06,551
另外一个头盔裂了
My other one of these cracked,

508
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,040
你用这个吧
so you can use this one.

509
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:09,440
好的
Okay.

510
00:17:10,041 --> 00:17:12,221
太好了 我们的乖女儿没疯
Yes! Our little girl isn't crazy!

511
00:17:12,221 --> 00:17:13,361
泰迪是真实存在的
Teddy's real!

512
00:17:13,361 --> 00:17:15,771
-是真的不像好人 -我去追
- Real freaky! - I'm going!

513
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:21,560
小卡 你在打鼾
Cam, you're snoring.

514
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:22,460
什么 不好意思
What? Sorry.

515
00:17:24,981 --> 00:17:25,942
是我打鼾吗
Was that me?

516
00:17:26,111 --> 00:17:27,681
天啊 天啊
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

517
00:17:28,140 --> 00:17:29,800
她在这里干什么
What is she doing out here?

518
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,280
-她的腿有睡眠不宁症 -两条都有吗
- Well, she has that restless leg. - Both of them?

519
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:33,480
天啊 把冰淇淋拿开
Oh, my gosh, get the ice cream!

520
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:36,240
我们要怎么办 该把她叫起来吗
What do we do? Should we wake her up?

521
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:37,420
然后说什么
And say what?

522
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:39,800
能烦请你从沙发上下来吗
"Would you mind terribly getting off our couch?

523
00:17:39,811 --> 00:17:40,951
你貌似在给它涂油
You seem to be glazing it."

524
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:42,300
你还有更好的主意吗
Do you have a better idea?

525
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:44,540
好吧 到后面去
Okay, okay, go around the back.

526
00:17:44,540 --> 00:17:45,560
我要怎么做 我要怎么做
What am I doing? What am I doing?

527
00:17:46,391 --> 00:17:48,331
把这个垫到她下面
We'll get this underneath her.

528
00:17:48,461 --> 00:17:51,221
有一次我帮一头母猪在我们家客厅地板上
Once, I helped a sow give birth to nine baby piglets

529
00:17:51,221 --> 00:17:52,011
给八只猪仔接生
on our living room floor.

530
00:17:52,011 --> 00:17:54,300
什么都没沾到油毯上
Didn't get a drop of nothin' on the linoleum.

531
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:56,050
等下再问你为什么客厅会有只母猪
We're gonna get back to why the sow was in the living room.

532
00:17:56,050 --> 00:17:57,760
我们一起看戴安娜王妃的婚礼直播 太美了
Lady Di's wedding. It was beautiful.

533
00:17:57,760 --> 00:17:59,060
小卡 我们会弄醒她的
Cam, she's gonna wake up.

534
00:17:59,060 --> 00:18:00,280
怎么可能 她吃了那么多安眠药
Oh, please, she's got enough pills in her,

535
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:01,830
多到可以像响葫芦一样摇响了
she's gonna rattle like a maraca.

536
00:18:01,830 --> 00:18:02,661
把她翻过来
Roll!

537
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:06,210
道格 不 我不想要
Doug, no, I don't wanna.

538
00:18:06,940 --> 00:18:08,320
好吧 我该怎么办 我该怎么办
Okay, okay, what do I do? What do I do?

539
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,560
你从这边过来
You come back around this way.

540
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:10,580
不 道格
No, Doug.

541
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:13,270
现在这么办 我把她往这边推
Now, what we're gonna do is I'll push her this way

542
00:18:13,270 --> 00:18:14,700
然后拉动毯子
and pull the blanket.

543
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:16,101
好 我得拉她是吗 好
Okay, I got to pull her? Okay.

544
00:18:18,890 --> 00:18:20,191
要掉了 要掉了
I'm losing her. I'm losing her.

545
00:18:23,230 --> 00:18:25,060
这样倒是也行 没问题的
This could work, too. It's fine.

546
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:30,850
怎 怎么了
What -- what happened?

547
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:32,100
你刚做恶梦了
You were having a really bad dream,

548
00:18:32,100 --> 00:18:33,020
然后沙发睡着也不太舒服
and then you rolled right off

549
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:34,400
你就滚下来了
of our uncomfortable sofa.

550
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:36,740
真抱歉 我太孤独了
I'm sorry. I-I was lonely.

551
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:38,140
我跑出来
I came out here,

552
00:18:38,140 --> 00:18:40,380
结果把你全家都吵醒了
and then I wound up waking up the whole house.

553
00:18:40,380 --> 00:18:42,580
我简直是世界上最讨人厌的客人
I'm the worst houseguest in the world!

554
00:18:42,580 --> 00:18:43,810
-别别别 -别别别
- Don't. - Don't.

555
00:18:43,810 --> 00:18:46,340
道格说得对 我会孤独终老的
Doug was right. I'm gonna die alone.

556
00:18:46,340 --> 00:18:47,740
-别别别 -别别别
- Don't. - Don't.

557
00:18:48,180 --> 00:18:49,140
过来
Okay, come on.

558
00:18:49,140 --> 00:18:51,100
你能不能安静点儿啊
Can you please be quiet?

559
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:54,060
真是太抱歉了 莉莉 都是我的错
I'm so sorry, Lily. It's all my fault.

560
00:18:54,060 --> 00:18:55,260
我头疼
My head hurts.

561
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:57,840
-我去给你拿点止疼药 -好
- I'm gonna get you some aspirin. - Okay.

562
00:18:59,579 --> 00:19:01,459
小卡 我们是不是太坏了
Cam, are we terrible people?

563
00:19:01,459 --> 00:19:03,459
还不是为了保护范德考夫的沙发
For protecting a Vanderkoff?

564
00:19:03,459 --> 00:19:04,579
他去年可是上吊自杀了
He hanged himself last year.

565
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:06,400
这玩意可是绝版 以后再也不会有了
It's not like they're making more of those.

566
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:08,060
我们刚刚把一个双相情感障碍的离婚妇女
We just rolled a bipolar divorcee

567
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:09,360
给滚到硬木地板上去了 还是脸先落地
face-first onto a hardwood floor.

568
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:10,240
就为了保护个沙发
All to protect a couch.

569
00:19:10,299 --> 00:19:12,849
不只是个沙发 那是我们唯一的好东西
It's not just a couch. Our one nice thing.

570
00:19:12,849 --> 00:19:15,869
我们过去七年一直用着这种油腻腻的台面
The last seven years have been about sticky countertops

571
00:19:15,869 --> 00:19:18,569
丑不拉几的浴帘 还有儿童安全锁
and horsy shower curtains and childproof locks.

572
00:19:18,569 --> 00:19:19,369
你知道这抽屉里是什么东西吗
Do you know what's in this drawer?

573
00:19:19,369 --> 00:19:20,119
我都不知道抽屉里是啥
I don't know what's in this drawer.

574
00:19:20,119 --> 00:19:20,669
完全不知道
I have no idea.

575
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:22,280
我知道这让人挺不爽的 好吧
Look, I know it's frustrating, all right?

576
00:19:22,409 --> 00:19:24,809
但这不是我们爱惜东西而不爱惜人的理由
But is that really a reason to choose a thing over a person?

577
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:26,960
拜托 我们简直跟道格是一个档次的
I mean, come on. We're no better than Doug.

578
00:19:28,879 --> 00:19:31,469
我觉得这对莉莉来说的确不是一个好榜样
I guess it's not a great example to set for Lily.

579
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:33,420
也许我们并不值得拥有这么一件好东西
Maybe we don't deserve one nice thing.

580
00:19:34,719 --> 00:19:37,279
然后太阳升起了 所有的乌龟
"And when the sun came out, all the turtles,

581
00:19:37,279 --> 00:19:40,218
从小A到小Z 都在野餐时愉快地玩耍
from Abner to Zeke, had fun at the picnic."

582
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:42,340
《乌龟们的下雨天》
"A rainy day for turtles."

583
00:19:43,488 --> 00:19:44,858
这本书总能让莉莉高兴起来
It always makes Lily feel better.

584
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:46,680
我想她是觉得...
I guess she just thought that...

585
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:48,480
我们确实拥有一样好东西
We do have one nice thing.

586
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:50,840
然后一场美丽的雨
"And a beautiful rain--"

587
00:19:52,618 --> 00:19:55,398
我们用不着非得看着它死去 走吧
Well, we don't have to watch it die. Come on.

588
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:00,300
走吧 杰
Let's go, Jay!

589
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:02,860
我们二十分钟后就该到野餐地点了
We're supposed to be at the picnic in 20 minutes!

590
00:20:02,860 --> 00:20:04,480
他们在货车里都住了六年
They've been living in a van for six years.

591
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:06,560
多等一小会儿也不会怎么样
They can wait a little longer.

592
00:20:07,158 --> 00:20:09,058
所以今天我是看不成球赛了
So, today, instead of watching the game,

593
00:20:09,058 --> 00:20:10,978
我得去跟哥伦比亚人在草地上玩飞镖
I'll be playing lawn darts with Colombians,

594
00:20:11,100 --> 00:20:12,960
谢谢你不长脑子
thanks to you not using your brain.

595
00:20:13,058 --> 00:20:14,108
我要看这个 《骗中骗》
Here we go -- "The Sting."

596
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:15,940
倒是有人是得偿所愿了
Well, someone's getting what they want today.

597
00:20:15,940 --> 00:20:18,600
你终于可以看你的宝贝电影了
You finally get to watch your precious movie, huh?

598
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:20,440
关于一场漫长骗局的传说
"A classic tale about a long con."

599
00:20:20,560 --> 00:20:21,120
我今天就让给你了
Well, you're welcome.

600
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:24,140
等一下
Wait a minute.

601
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:25,880
流氓和出卖朋友的人遍地都是
"Rogues and double-crossers abound.

602
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:27,320
谁能胜过谁
Who will outsmart whom?"

603
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:28,380
混蛋
Son of a bitch.

604
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:30,780
你知道我利用狗狗成人礼派对
You knew I was using the bark mitzvah

605
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:32,200
当做讨价还价的筹码
as a bargaining chip.

606
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:34,400
所以你才说服歌洛丽亚回去
That's why you talked Gloria into coming back --

607
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,980
所以我就逃不掉这个野餐
So I couldn't weasel my way out of this stupid picnic

608
00:20:37,097 --> 00:20:38,857
然后你就能独占大电视
and you'd get the big TV.

609
00:20:38,857 --> 00:20:40,378
我现在盯上你了
Well, I'm onto you now.

610
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:43,480
我只不过是在读DVD封面
I was just reading off the DVD box.

611
00:20:46,857 --> 00:20:48,327
你能相信吗
I mean, can you believe

612
00:20:48,327 --> 00:20:50,107
布伦达过来住一晚上就带这么多东西
all the stuff Brenda brought for one night?

613
00:20:50,107 --> 00:20:52,077
是啊 看那一堆东西
I know. Look at all this stuff over here.

614
00:20:52,077 --> 00:20:53,817
超补水唇膏
Super replenishing balm?

615
00:20:53,817 --> 00:20:56,437
毛孔收缩精华液
Uh, pore-reducing booster serum?

616
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:58,660
抗老化提亮珠珠
Anti-aging buffing beads?

617
00:20:58,907 --> 00:21:00,867
当女人也太累了
It must be so hard to be a girl.

618
00:21:00,867 --> 00:21:01,917
可不是嘛
I know. I know.

619
00:21:01,917 --> 00:21:03,287
真让人担心以后莉莉要怎样
It really makes you worry about the world

620
00:21:03,287 --> 00:21:04,407
应付这个不友好的世界
we're sending Lily out into.

621
00:21:04,407 --> 00:21:06,667
女孩必须要完美无缺 这压力太大了
Well, there's so much pressure on girls to be perfect.

622
00:21:06,740 --> 00:21:07,960
-你好了吗 -好了
- You ready? - Yep.

623
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:09,760
问题是 小卡
The thing is, Cam,

624
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:11,640
我们能做的就是把我们的价值观教给她
all we can do is instill our beliefs in her

625
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:13,300
期望她能做出明智的选择
and hope that she makes good choices.

626
00:21:13,300 --> 00:21:14,320
镇静喷雾要么[冷静点了吗]
Calming mister?

627
00:21:14,377 --> 00:21:15,787
这么谈一谈确实好多了
It does feel nice to talk about it.

628
00:21:15,787 --> 00:21:17,307
不是 这是个镇静喷雾
No, this is a calming mister.

629
00:21:17,307 --> 00:21:18,077
我刚买的
I just bought this.

630
00:21:18,077 --> 00:21:18,877
哦是吗 要的
Oh, god, yes.

631
00:21:18,877 --> 00:21:19,788
试试
Wanna try it?
